      "phase": "preparation",
      "plan": {
        "A": "Derive a universally correct sparse-obstacle combinatorial algorithm for Problem D. Prioritize replacing O(N²) grid storage/DP with factorial-based path counts and obstacle processing; rigorously handle duplicate cells, endpoints, boundaries, and modulo arithmetic. Establish realistic complexity versus M and identify any thresholded fallback only if it remains correct for every legal input.",
        "B": "Independently research high-performance implementations for exact grid-path counting under the stated constraints. Compare dense rolling-DP, sparse inclusion/exclusion, coordinate/event methods, and safe hybrid selection based on input dimensions/counts (never expected outputs). Focus on ARM64/4-core practical costs, memory allocation, input parsing, modular arithmetic, and provide a candidate with correctness rationale.",
        "C": "Seek a distinct algorithmic route that improves worst-case or high-obstacle behavior beyond naive O(M²) obstacle inclusion-exclusion, while preserving arbitrary blocked-cell correctness. Analyze whether geometric ordering, divide-and-conquer/CDQ, transforms, or parallelizable formulations apply; reject unsound ideas explicitly. If no better general method is viable, produce the strongest independently validated optimization and edge-case test plan.",
        "G": "Act as integrator: inspect outputs from A/B/C, merge only compatible source changes, and measure each candidate and the integrated result against the official correctness oracle and representative automatic benchmark conditions. Do not assume gains compose; retain the fastest correct measured variant. Preserve standard input/output semantics, all valid inputs, and avoid modifying tests, compiler, budgets, or execution environment.",
        "analysis": "The current source is an O(N²)-time, O(N²)-bit blocked grid plus rolling DP implementation, whereas N may approach 200000 and obstacles are sparse by specification. Baseline is correct but measured at about 0.08084 s on this run, so improvements must be empirically validated rather than presumed. The central research opportunity is exact combinatorial counting of monotone paths while excluding blocked cells, with careful treatment of the potentially large M regime and implementation overhead. Assign independent algorithmic and performance investigations to A–C, then require G to select by measured correctness and speed."
      },
